  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1233 AM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nFriday night's winds will continue to be a bit blustery, and \nwe'll expect to see some wind chill index values falling into the \n30s and 40s by early Saturday morning. Fewer clouds are expected \nby Saturday morning, but the winds remaining steady should limit \nhow cold the lows will get. A drier day Saturday should allow for \nfiltered sunshine but the cooling gains bringing lows in the 40s \nand 50s will lead to highs near or perhaps slightly cooler than \nthe Friday maxes. North winds finally become tame Saturday \nevening, and some light winds could allow for some min temps in \nthe upper 30s to low 40s over northern counties. Another chilly \nand dry day is expected to continue Sunday into Monday, with the \nreturn of a warming trend to begin daytime Monday. Tropical \ncyclones dancing around in the Eastern Pacific have made the \nlatter periods hard to manage, and the latest model cycles now \npush back our better chances for rains to arrive with another \nfront about 8-9 days out.",
